// F28: one pilot run brute-forced eight names before reaching `fs.write_text`. Edit distance
// cannot find it -- `write` to `write_text` is five inserts -- so the prefix is what gets matched,
// and several are offered, because choosing between _text and _bytes is a choice a reader can make.
//
// **Four of them, and the number is load-bearing.** The list is the first matches in declaration
// order, so when `fs` gained `write_text_private` the cap of three pushed `write_bytes` off the end
// and this diagnostic began offering three ways to write text and no way to write bytes -- losing
// the one choice it exists to put in front of a reader. The cap went to four rather than the
// golden being updated to the worse list.
use fs

fn main() {
    val r = fs.write("greeting.txt", "hello")
}
